---

## Critical Rules During Migration

1. **Never delete without verifying migration is complete.** Always backup before removing.
2. **WAI-MIGRATION.yaml is the source of truth.** Update it after every phase closeout with the commit hash.
3. **Existing Lug content is sacred.** Add fields, never remove.
4. **WAI-Guide.md and BRIEF.md migrate byte-for-byte.**
5. **Every phase must closeout with a git commit and updated WAI-MIGRATION.yaml.**
6. **If you see retired_files in WAI-MIGRATION.yaml, do not read or write them.**

---

## What "Retired" Means

- `WAI-Signals.jsonl` — RETIRED. Tombstoned. Signals are now Lugs with `impact >= 8`. Do not write to this file.
- `WAI-Backpressure.yaml` — Will be RETIRED in Phase 3. Becomes a `qc-check` Skill.

---

## v2 Schema Changes (What Is Different Now)

All `WAI-Lugs.jsonl` files have been migrated. Lugs now have:
- Full field names (`id`, `type`, `title`, `status`) instead of shorthand (`i`, `ty`, `t`, `s`)
- `impact` (1-10 integer) — required
- `created_by` (string) — required
- `node` (string, e.g. `wheelwright/framework`) — required
- `created_at` (ISO 8601) — required
- `perceive`, `execute`, `verify` (optional PEV fields, null by default)
- `resolution`, `resolution_reason` (calibration fields, null until resolved)
- `_v1_status` — preserved original status value for backward reference

Status values are now: `published`, `in_progress`, `resolved`, `acknowledged`, `draft`
(Old values `open`, `in-progress`, `closed` were mapped and preserved in `_v1_status`)
